bic_trace_step.reason:
In drbd_adm_dump_devices(), before acquiring rcu_read_lock(), the code does:
  resource = drbd_find_resource(nla_data(resource_filter));
  if (!resource) goto put_result;
If drbd_find_resource() returns NULL, execution jumps to 'put_result', which eventually falls through to 'out' where rcu_read_unlock() is called. Since rcu_read_lock() was never acquired, this creates an unbalanced RCU lock/unlock. The same pattern exists in drbd_adm_dump_peer_devices(). No fix (e.g., moving the check after rcu_read_lock() or adding a separate error path) is present in this commit.
